+# Contract: Full-Text Search Feature
+
+## Search Endpoint: `GET /notes/search?q=<query>`
+
+### Behaviors
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| S1 | Returns 200 with matching results for keyword query | `GET /notes/search?q=python` → 200, `results.length > 0` |
+| S2 | Results include `snippet` field with string value | `results[0].snippet` is a string |
+| S3 | Snippets contain `<mark>` and `</mark>` around matched terms | `snippet.includes('<mark>') && snippet.includes('</mark>')` |
+| S4 | Results ranked by relevance (BM25 ascending) | For query "programming", `results[i].rank >= results[i-1].rank` |
+| S5 | Supports quoted phrase queries | `?q="chocolate chip"` returns matching notes |
+| S6 | Results contain id, title, snippet, rank (all correct types) | Each result has number id, string title, string snippet, number rank |
+| S7 | Returns empty array for nonexistent terms | `?q=xyznonexistentterm` → 200, `results = []` |
+| S8 | Returns 400 when `q` parameter is missing | `GET /notes/search` → 400 |
+| S9 | Returns 400 when `q` is empty string | `?q=` → 400 |
+| S10 | Pagination: default 20 per page, controlled by `?page=N` | `?q=the&page=1` → `results.length <= 20`, `page: 1`, `perPage: 20` |
+| S11 | Pagination: page=2 returns next page of results | `?q=the&page=2` → `page: 2`, `results` is array (possibly empty) |
+| S12 | Response includes `total` count | `response.body` has `total` (number > 0 for matching query) |
+
+## Suggest Endpoint: `GET /notes/search/suggest?q=<prefix>`
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| G1 | Returns up to 5 matching note titles | `?q=learn` → `results.length <= 5 && results.length > 0` |
+| G2 | Results match prefix in title | `?q=getting` → a title includes "getting" (case-insensitive) |
+| G3 | Returns 400 when `q` is empty | `?q=` → 400 |
+| G4 | Returns 400 when `q` is missing | `GET /notes/search/suggest` → 400 |
+
+## FTS Index Synchronization
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| C1 | FTS syncs on create: new note appears in search immediately | Create note with unique term "zylophone", then search → finds it |
+| C2 | FTS syncs on update: updated content appears, old content disappears | Create note → update with unique term "xylographics" → search finds it, old term "elephants" gone |
+| C3 | FTS syncs on delete: deleted note disappears from search | Create with "quizzaciously" → verify found → delete → verify gone |
+
+## Robustness
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| R1 | Special characters in query don't crash | Test `hello%20world`, `test%26test`, `it%27s`, `%3Cscript%3E`, `foo%2Bbar`, `a%2Fb` → all return 200 with results array |
+| R2 | Search completes in under 100ms for seeded dataset | `?q=programming` on seeded DB → `elapsed < 100ms` |
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| B1 | All 15 existing CRUD tests continue to pass | `npm test` → 15 notes tests pass |
+| B2 | All 5 existing CRUD operations work correctly | GET list, GET by id, POST, PUT, DELETE all work |
+| B3 | Tag filtering still works | `?tag=X` filter on GET /notes |
